# Pololu Isolated USB-to-I2C Adapter -> /dev/ttyMAG0 udev rule.
#
# The Pololu vendor publishes two variants of the adapter:
#     USB\VID_1FFB&PID_2502  -- 5396 (no isolated power)
#     USB\VID_1FFB&PID_2503  -- 5397 (with isolated power)
#
# Either presents on Linux as a cdc_acm device (/dev/ttyACMn).  This
# rule pins both variants to a stable name (/dev/ttyMAG0) and sets
# group ownership to dialout so a non-root user in that group can
# open the port without sudo.
#
# $ lsusb
# Bus 003 Device 023: ID 1ffb:2503 Pololu Corporation
#     Pololu Isolated USB-to-I2C Adapter with Isolated Power
#
# Install:
#   sudo cp install/99-PololuI2C.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
#
# Verify after replug:
#   ls -l /dev/ttyMAG0   # -> ttyACMx, root:dialout, mode 0660
#
# The rules also TAG the device for systemd and name mag-recorder.service in
# SYSTEMD_WANTS, so attaching the adapter starts the recorder immediately.
#
# That is the other half of `ConditionPathExists=/dev/ttyMAG0` in
# systemd/mag-recorder.service.  The condition stops a station with no
# magnetometer from crash-looping the unit to start-limit-hit at every boot
# (WB6CXC-7 and W3USR-06, 2026-10-02: all ten of StartLimitBurst spent in
# ~74 s).  But a condition is only evaluated when something TRIES to start the
# unit, so on its own it would turn "plug the sensor in" into "plug the sensor
# in, then reboot".  SYSTEMD_WANTS closes that: udev starts the unit on device
# arrival, the condition then passes, and the recorder comes up on its own.
#
# ⚠ Keep the two in step.  If the symlink name here ever changes, the
# ConditionPathExists in the unit must change with it, or the unit silently
# never starts.
KERNEL=="ttyACM[0-9]*", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1ffb", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2502", SYMLINK+="ttyMAG0", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="mag-recorder.service"
KERNEL=="ttyACM[0-9]*", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1ffb", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2503", SYMLINK+="ttyMAG0", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="mag-recorder.service"
